{
    "background_story": "Nixon was a charismatic and eccentric performer who made a name for himself in the city's underground theater scene. By day, he worked as a humble costume designer, but by night, he transformed into a dazzling spectacle. Donning elaborate, handmade costumes, Nixon would take to the stage, mesmerizing audiences with his androgynous charm and acrobatic feats. His most famous character, 'The Phantom Siren,' was a costumed alter ego that blended elements of mythology and steampunk. Nixon's love of costuming was not just about aesthetics; it was a way for him to tap into different personas and explore the depths of human emotion. As his fame grew, so did his wardrobe, with each new creation more breathtaking than the last. Nixon's art was a testament to the power of self-expression and the magic of transformation.",
